<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashikaga Shigeuji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1438–1497</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashikaga Shigeuji was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-mochiuji">Ashikaga Mochiuji</a> and was restored as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> kubo in 1449. In 1454 he had the Kanto deputy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-noritada">Uesugi Noritada</a> killed, starting the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyotoku-war">Kyōtoku War</a>. Driven from Kamakura, he moved to Koga in 1455, where he and his heirs ruled as the Koga kubo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashikaga-shigeuji.jpg" alt="Ashikaga Shigeuji" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Kunisada II · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashikaga_Shigeuji_Koga_Kubo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
